From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 01:16:47 -0400
Subject: keys: Arc's keyboard for Spaces, copy link, the shortcut reference

Ctrl-1..9, Option-Cmd-Left/Right, Shift-Cmd-K, Cmd-D and
Option-Shift-Cmd-Left/Right drive Spaces from the keyboard and a Spaces
menu in the menu bar (docs/features/spaces.md B18-B23, B28-B30); tab
traversal moves to Option-Cmd-Up/Down and pane focus to F6. Shift-Cmd-C
copies the page's link without tracking parameters, Option-Shift-Cmd-C as a
Markdown link with a rich-text twin (docs/features/copy-link.md), with a
toast; both join the tab menu, the File menu and the app menu. The Stedding
settings section gains a read-only Shortcuts block built from the
accelerator tables (docs/features/shortcuts.md), a toggle for the tracking
strip, one for motion, and every Stedding string this fork adds now lives in
chrome/app/stedding_strings.grdp. The welcome flow's key step lists the new
chords and links to the reference.

Why: docs/ROUND6-PLAN.md wave 1 (R6-01, R6-02, R6-04): Arc parity for the
keyboard, and an in-product shortcut reference that cannot drift from the
binary.
Removable when: Chromium offers per-window Spaces with chords of its own and
a shortcut reference page.
